            B.q("ai-m4-19", "ai-cosmos-perf", "Data is partitioned by /tenantId, and the largest tenant is nearing the 20 GB limit for one logical partition (all items sharing one partition key value). What lets this tenant keep growing while queries can still target one tenant?", listOf("Increase the RU/s so the logical partition splits across physical partitions", "Move to a new container partitioned by a synthetic key that joins tenantId and userId", "Move to a new container with hierarchical partition keys, such as /tenantId then /userId", "Enable the analytical store so older records move out of the partition"), setOf(2), "A logical partition can hold at most 20 GB. Hierarchical partition keys (subpartitioning) split a tenant's data by a second and even third key, so a big tenant spreads across many partitions while queries on tenantId alone still go only to that tenant's partitions.",
