            B.q("ai-m4-22", "ai-cosmos-changefeed", "A Cosmos DB trigger re-embeds a product when its description changes and saves the vector back onto the same item. The function now fires in an endless loop. Which two changes stop it? Select two.", listOf("Store a hash of the text the embedding was made from, and skip items whose current text hash equals it", "Write embeddings to a separate container instead of back onto the monitored item", "Set the trigger's start time to now", "Delete the lease container"), setOf(0, 1), "Saving the embedding is itself an update, so it appears in the change feed and triggers the function again. Either detect that the text has not changed (compare a stored hash) or write the vector somewhere the trigger is not watching.",
