            B.q("ai-m4-26", "ai-postgres", "Sign-in looks up users with WHERE lower(email) = lower(%s), and an index on email is never used. What index helps?", listOf("A GIN index: CREATE INDEX ON users USING gin (to_tsvector('simple', email))", "A covering index: CREATE INDEX ON users (email) INCLUDE (id)", "An expression index: CREATE INDEX ON users (lower(email))", "A hash index: CREATE INDEX ON users USING hash (email)"), setOf(2), "An index on email stores the original values, so a filter on lower(email) cannot use it. An expression index stores lower(email) itself, matching the query exactly.",
